  "researchNote": "The South Carolina National Guard's own site (scguard.com) now resolves to an unrelated parked/expired domain, and no South Carolina Military Department awards regulation or statute could be located. Award names come from the unsourced South Carolina section of Wikipedia's 'List of decorations awarded by the United States National Guard' cross-checked against USA Military Medals (usamm.com) current product listings, which independently confirm 8 of 12 names as real, currently-sold ribbons (Safety Ribbon, Achievement Ribbon, Palmetto Service Ribbon, Retirement Medal, Counter-Drug Ribbon, Recruiting and Retention Ribbon, Active State Service Ribbon, Palmetto Cross Medal). Several USAMM product descriptions state a relative wear order (e.g. 'Worn before the SC Counter-Drug Ribbon', 'Worn after the SC NG Achievement Medal') but these are the retailer's own descriptive copy, not an official regulation, so they were not used to assign inStatePrecedence. Neither lead is a .mil/.gov/regulation source, so the file and every entry are flagged needs-source.",
